<div id="p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p">The appendix is divided into the following parts.
Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Omitted Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>: Omitted proofs and theoretical results; Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Additional Discussion and Experimental Setup ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>: additional discussions and details on the experimental setup; and Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Additional Experiments and Ablation Studies ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>: Additional empirical results and ablation studies.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Omitted Proofs and Theoretical Results</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first introduce (and prove) the following useful lemmas that are related in the main text and that facilitate the proofs of the propositions.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="Thmlem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmlem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmlem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-exponential and <math id="Thmlem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-logarithm are generalizations of the exponential and logarithm functions since <math id="Thmlem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\alpha\to 1}\exp_{\alpha}(z)=\exp(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>exp</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\alpha\to 1}\exp_{\alpha}(z)=\exp(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\alpha\to 1}\log_{\alpha}(z)=\log(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\alpha\to 1}\log_{\alpha}(z)=\log(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim\limits_{t\to 1}(1+tz)^{1/t}=\exp(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim\limits_{t\to 1}(1+tz)^{1/t}=\exp(z)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim\limits_{\alpha\to 1}\exp_{\alpha}(z)=\lim\limits_{\alpha\to 1}(1+(\alpha-1)z)^{1/(\alpha-1)}=\exp(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>exp</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim\limits_{\alpha\to 1}\exp_{\alpha}(z)=\lim\limits_{\alpha\to 1}(1+(\alpha-1)z)^{1/(\alpha-1)}=\exp(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Similarly for <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-logarithm, by the L’Hôpital’s rule,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E1X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{\alpha\to 1}\log_{\alpha}(t)=\lim_{\alpha\to 1}\frac{t^{\alpha-1}-1}{\alpha-1}=\lim_{\beta\to 0}\frac{t^{\beta}-1}{\beta}=\lim_{\beta\to 0}\frac{e^{\beta\log(t)}-1}{\beta}=\log(t)\lim_{\beta\to 0}\frac{e^{\beta\log(t)}-1}{\beta\log(t)}=\log(t)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{\alpha\to 1}\log_{\alpha}(t)=\lim_{\alpha\to 1}\frac{t^{\alpha-1}-1}{\alpha-1}=\lim_{\beta\to 0}\frac{t^{\beta}-1}{\beta}=\lim_{\beta\to 0}\frac{e^{\beta\log(t)}-1}{\beta}=\log(t)\lim_{\beta\to 0}\frac{e^{\beta\log(t)}-1}{\beta\log(t)}=\log(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.2</span></span><span id="Thmlem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Hölder’s inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ledoux, 2001</a>)</cite>)<span id="Thmlem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in[1,\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in[1,\infty]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmlem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{p}+\frac{1}{q}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{p}+\frac{1}{q}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then for all real-valued functions <math id="Thmlem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> measurable with respect to measure <math id="Thmlem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|fg\|_{L^{1}(\mu)}\leq\|f\|_{L^{p}(\mu)}\|g\|_{L^{q}(\mu)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|fg\|_{L^{1}(\mu)}\leq\|f\|_{L^{p}(\mu)}\|g\|_{L^{q}(\mu)}</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="Thmlem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=q=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=q=2</annotation></semantics></math>, the Hölder’s inequality degenerates to the Cauchy–Schwarz inequality.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmprop1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 2 Taxonomy of Inference-Time Alignment through Regret Analysis ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following the definition of the inference-time regret, we decompose it using <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\textsf{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\textsf{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> as an anchor policy,</p>
<table id="A1.E2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E2X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{regret}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗀𝗋𝖾𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{regret}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=J_{r^{*}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{r^{*}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=J_{r^{*}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{r^{*}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.2)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E2Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{J_{r^{*}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)}_{(i)}-\underbrace{\left(J_{r^{*}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right)}_{(ii)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{J_{r^{*}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)}_{(i)}-\underbrace{\left(J_{r^{*}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right)}_{(ii)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed, hence once <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\textsf{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\textsf{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> is selected, term (i) becomes a baseline sub-optimality constant that characterize how far the reference is from optimal under the true reward, and is independent of the inference-time alignment mechanism.
Using the definition of the expected density ratio, term (i) can be upper bounded by</p>
<table id="A1.E3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E3X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{r^{*}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{r^{*}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(J_{\hat{r}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right)-\left(J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(J_{\hat{r}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right)-\left(J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlem2" title="Lemma A.2 (Hölder’s inequality ( , )). ‣ Appendix A Omitted Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.E4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E4X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}-r^{*}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}-r^{*}\right]\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>]</mo><mo fence="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}-r^{*}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}-r^{*}\right]\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.4)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E4Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(\cdot|x)}\left[\left(\frac{\pi^{*}}{\pi_{\textsf{ref}}}-1\right)\left(\hat{r}-r^{*}\right)\right]\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo fence="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(\cdot|x)}\left[\left(\frac{\pi^{*}}{\pi_{\textsf{ref}}}-1\right)\left(\hat{r}-r^{*}\right)\right]\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E4Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{C^{\pi^{*}}-1}\times\epsilon_{2}(\hat{r};\pi_{\textsf{ref}},x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{C^{\pi^{*}}-1}\times\epsilon_{2}(\hat{r};\pi_{\textsf{ref}},x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Similarly, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|J_{\hat{r}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)|\leq\sqrt{C^{\pi^{*}}-1}\times\|\hat{r}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|J_{\hat{r}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)|\leq\sqrt{C^{\pi^{*}}-1}\times\|\hat{r}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}})}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Putting them together, term (i) can be upper bounded by</p>
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E5X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{r^{*}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{r^{*}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left|J_{\hat{r}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right|+\left|J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left|J_{\hat{r}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right|+\left|J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi^{*};x)-J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.5)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E5Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{C^{\pi^{*}}-1}\left(\epsilon_{2}(\hat{r};\pi_{\textsf{ref}},x)+\|\hat{r}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{C^{\pi^{*}}-1}\left(\epsilon_{2}(\hat{r};\pi_{\textsf{ref}},x)+\|\hat{r}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Next, for term (ii), it can be similarly decompose into</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{r^{*}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{r^{*}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(J_{\hat{r}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right)+\left(J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(J_{\hat{r}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right)+\left(J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.6)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E6Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\left(J_{\hat{r}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right)-\left|J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\left(J_{\hat{r}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right)-\left|J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r},r^{*}\in[0,R_{\textsf{max}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r},r^{*}\in[0,R_{\textsf{max}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E7X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{\hat{r}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{\hat{r}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=J_{\hat{r}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{w};x)+J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=J_{\hat{r}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{w};x)+J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.7)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E7Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Delta(\pi_{w})+J_{\hat{r}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{w};x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Delta(\pi_{w})+J_{\hat{r}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}}(\pi_{w};x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E7Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\Delta(\pi_{w})-2R_{\textsf{max}}D_{\textsf{TV}}(\hat{\pi}_{w}\|\pi_{w})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">max</mtext></msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">TV</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\Delta(\pi_{w})-2R_{\textsf{max}}D_{\textsf{TV}}(\hat{\pi}_{w}\|\pi_{w}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Then, by Lemma <a href="#Thmlem2" title="Lemma A.2 (Hölder’s inequality ( , )). ‣ Appendix A Omitted Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> again, we have</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E8X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)-J_{\hat{r}-r^{*}}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}};x)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(1+(\alpha-1)D_{\alpha}(\pi_{w}\|\pi_{\textsf{ref}})\right)^{1/\alpha}\|\hat{r}-r^{*}\|_{L^{\beta}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(1+(\alpha-1)D_{\alpha}(\pi_{w}\|\pi_{\textsf{ref}})\right)^{1/\alpha}\|\hat{r}-r^{*}\|_{L^{\beta}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.8)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E8Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{C^{\pi_{w}}}\times\epsilon_{2}(\hat{r};\pi_{\textsf{ref}},x)\;\text{if selecting $\alpha=\beta=2$}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msup><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msup></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>if selecting </mtext><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{C^{\pi_{w}}}\times\epsilon_{2}(\hat{r};\pi_{\textsf{ref}},x)\;\text{if selecting $\alpha=\beta=2$}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.6" class="ltx_p">Combining Eq. (<a href="#A1.E5" title="Equation A.5 ‣ A.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Omitted Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>), Eq. (<a href="#A1.E7" title="Equation A.7 ‣ A.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Omitted Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A1.E8" title="Equation A.8 ‣ A.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Omitted Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E9X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{regret}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗋𝖾𝗀𝗋𝖾𝗍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{regret}(\hat{\pi}_{w};x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{C^{\pi^{*}}-1}\left(\epsilon_{2}(\hat{r};\pi_{\textsf{ref}},x)+\|\hat{r}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}})}\right)-\Delta(\pi_{w})+2R_{\textsf{max}}D_{\textsf{TV}}(\hat{\pi}_{w}\|\pi_{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">max</mtext></msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">TV</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{C^{\pi^{*}}-1}\left(\epsilon_{2}(\hat{r};\pi_{\textsf{ref}},x)+\|\hat{r}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}})}\right)-\Delta(\pi_{w})+2R_{\textsf{max}}D_{\textsf{TV}}(\hat{\pi}_{w}\|\pi_{w})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.9)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E9Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\left(1+(\alpha-1)D_{\alpha}(\pi_{w}\|\pi_{\textsf{ref}})\right)^{1/\alpha}\|\hat{r}-r^{*}\|_{L^{\beta}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\left(1+(\alpha-1)D_{\alpha}(\pi_{w}\|\pi_{\textsf{ref}})\right)^{1/\alpha}\|\hat{r}-r^{*}\|_{L^{\beta}(\pi_{\textsf{ref}})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.7" class="ltx_p">Taking <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\beta=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\beta=2</annotation></semantics></math> leads to the desired result.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmprop2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ 3.2 Light vs. Heavy Tails: When to be Optimistic? ‣ 3 Reward Tails and Alignment Regret ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a prompt <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and suppress the conditioning on it.
Let the proxy reward be <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}:=\hat{r}(x,Y)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}:=\hat{r}(x,Y)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\sim\pi_{\textsf{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\sim\pi_{\textsf{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We define the endpoint gap <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U:=1-\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U:=1-\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By assumption:</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\sim\text{Beta}\left(\frac{1}{\kappa},1\right),\quad\text{with density }f_{U}(u)=\frac{1}{\kappa}u^{\frac{1}{\kappa}-1}\text{ for }u\in[0,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Beta</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>with density </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\sim\text{Beta}\left(\frac{1}{\kappa},1\right),\quad\text{with density }f_{U}(u)=\frac{1}{\kappa}u^{\frac{1}{\kappa}-1}\text{ for }u\in[0,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We utilize the general regret bound decomposition derived previously, where the regret <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the <span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Peak</span> (relative supremum), <span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dist</span> (distortion), and <span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gain</span> (<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>) of the weighting function <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\hat{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\hat{r})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(\pi)\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{N}{\text{Peak}(w)}\right)+\epsilon\cdot\text{Dist}(w)-\Delta(w)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mtext>Peak</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>Dist</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(\pi)\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{N}{\text{Peak}(w)}\right)+\epsilon\cdot\text{Dist}(w)-\Delta(w).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The statistics are defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Peak}(w)=\frac{\sup_{\hat{r}}w(\hat{r})}{\mathbb{E}[w(\hat{r})]},\;\text{Dist}(w)=\frac{\sqrt{\mathbb{E}[w(\hat{r})^{2}]}}{\mathbb{E}[w(\hat{r})]},\;\Delta(w)=\Delta(\pi_{w})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{w}}[\hat{r}]-\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Peak</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Dist</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Peak}(w)=\frac{\sup_{\hat{r}}w(\hat{r})}{\mathbb{E}[w(\hat{r})]},\;\text{Dist}(w)=\frac{\sqrt{\mathbb{E}[w(\hat{r})^{2}]}}{\mathbb{E}[w(\hat{r})]},\;\Delta(w)=\Delta(\pi_{w})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{w}}[\hat{r}]-\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Preliminaries: Moments.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\sim\text{Beta}(1/\kappa,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Beta</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\sim\text{Beta}(1/\kappa,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the raw moments are given by:</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[U^{m}]=\int_{0}^{1}u^{m}\frac{1}{\kappa}u^{\frac{1}{\kappa}-1}du=\frac{1}{m\kappa+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[U^{m}]=\int_{0}^{1}u^{m}\frac{1}{\kappa}u^{\frac{1}{\kappa}-1}du=\frac{1}{m\kappa+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This implies that in the heavy-tail regime (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> remains distributed over <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> but with mean <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 1/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 1/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>. In the light-tail regime (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}=1-U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}=1-U</annotation></semantics></math> concentrates near 0 with moments:</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}]=1-\mathbb{E}[U]=\frac{\kappa}{\kappa+1},\quad\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}^{2}]=1-\frac{2}{\kappa+1}+\frac{1}{2\kappa+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}]=1-\mathbb{E}[U]=\frac{\kappa}{\kappa+1},\quad\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}^{2}]=1-\frac{2}{\kappa+1}+\frac{1}{2\kappa+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, for each fixed integer <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}^{m}]=m!\kappa^{m}+O(\kappa^{m+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}^{m}]=m!\kappa^{m}+O(\kappa^{m+1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Part 1: Heavy-tailed regime (large <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we analyze the statistics using <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> as the primary variable.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">1.1 Soft-BoN.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The weight is <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{\textsf{sBoN}}(\hat{r})=e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}=e^{(1-U)/\lambda}\propto e^{-U/\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">sBoN</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\textsf{sBoN}}(\hat{r})=e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}=e^{(1-U)/\lambda}\propto e^{-U/\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{w}(U)=e^{-U/\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{w}(U)=e^{-U/\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Peak:</span>
We expand the expectation of the weight using Taylor series:</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[e^{-U/\lambda}]=1-\frac{1}{\lambda}\mathbb{E}[U]+O(\mathbb{E}[U^{2}])=1-\frac{1}{\lambda(\kappa+1)}+O(\kappa^{-2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[e^{-U/\lambda}]=1-\frac{1}{\lambda}\mathbb{E}[U]+O(\mathbb{E}[U^{2}])=1-\frac{1}{\lambda(\kappa+1)}+O(\kappa^{-2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The Peak is the ratio of the supremum (at <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=0</annotation></semantics></math>) to the expectation:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Peak}=\frac{1}{\mathbb{E}[e^{-U/\lambda}]}=\frac{1}{1-\frac{1}{\lambda\kappa}+o(\kappa^{-1})}=1+\frac{1}{\lambda\kappa}+o(\kappa^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Peak</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Peak}=\frac{1}{\mathbb{E}[e^{-U/\lambda}]}=\frac{1}{1-\frac{1}{\lambda\kappa}+o(\kappa^{-1})}=1+\frac{1}{\lambda\kappa}+o(\kappa^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting this into the exponential term in Eq. (<a href="#A1.E11" title="Equation A.11 ‣ A.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Omitted Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(-\frac{N}{\text{Peak}}\right)\approx\exp\left(-\frac{N}{1+1/(\lambda\kappa)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mtext>Peak</mtext></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(-\frac{N}{\text{Peak}}\right)\approx\exp\left(-\frac{N}{1+1/(\lambda\kappa)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dist.:</span>
We compute the second moment <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[w^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[w^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{w}^{2}=e^{-2U/\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>U</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{w}^{2}=e^{-2U/\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[e^{-2U/\lambda}]=1-\frac{2}{\lambda\kappa}+\frac{2}{\lambda^{2}(2\kappa)}+o(\kappa^{-1})=1-\frac{2}{\lambda\kappa}+\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}\kappa}+o(\kappa^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>U</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[e^{-2U/\lambda}]=1-\frac{2}{\lambda\kappa}+\frac{2}{\lambda^{2}(2\kappa)}+o(\kappa^{-1})=1-\frac{2}{\lambda\kappa}+\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}\kappa}+o(\kappa^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The squared distortion is:</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Dist}^{2}=\frac{\mathbb{E}[e^{-2U/\lambda}]}{(\mathbb{E}[e^{-U/\lambda}])^{2}}\approx\frac{1-\frac{2}{\lambda\kappa}+\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}\kappa}}{1-\frac{2}{\lambda\kappa}+\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}\kappa}(\frac{1}{2})}\approx 1+\frac{1}{2\lambda^{2}\kappa}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext>Dist</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>U</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Dist}^{2}=\frac{\mathbb{E}[e^{-2U/\lambda}]}{(\mathbb{E}[e^{-U/\lambda}])^{2}}\approx\frac{1-\frac{2}{\lambda\kappa}+\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}\kappa}}{1-\frac{2}{\lambda\kappa}+\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}\kappa}(\frac{1}{2})}\approx 1+\frac{1}{2\lambda^{2}\kappa}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Dist}\approx 1+\frac{1}{4\lambda^{2}\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Dist</mtext><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Dist}\approx 1+\frac{1}{4\lambda^{2}\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gain:</span>
The proxy gain is <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\mathbb{E}[U]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{w}}[U]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\mathbb{E}[U]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{w}}[U]</annotation></semantics></math>.
We compute the tilted expectation <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{w}}[U]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{w}}[U]</annotation></semantics></math> using the substitution <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\kappa U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\kappa U</annotation></semantics></math> (approximating <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> as Exponential<math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1/\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1/\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Ue^{-U/\lambda}]\approx\int_{0}^{\infty}ue^{-u/\lambda}\frac{1}{\kappa}e^{-u/\kappa}du\approx\frac{1}{\kappa}\int_{0}^{1}ue^{-u/\lambda}du." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≈</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mi>u</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Ue^{-U/\lambda}]\approx\int_{0}^{\infty}ue^{-u/\lambda}\frac{1}{\kappa}e^{-u/\kappa}du\approx\frac{1}{\kappa}\int_{0}^{1}ue^{-u/\lambda}du.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A precise integration yields <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{w}}[U]\approx\frac{\lambda}{\kappa}(1-e^{-1/\lambda})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{w}}[U]\approx\frac{\lambda}{\kappa}(1-e^{-1/\lambda})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus:</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta\approx\frac{1}{\kappa}-\frac{\lambda}{\kappa}(1-e^{-1/\lambda})=\frac{1}{\kappa}\left(1-\lambda(1-e^{-1/\lambda})\right)+o(\kappa^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\approx\frac{1}{\kappa}-\frac{\lambda}{\kappa}(1-e^{-1/\lambda})=\frac{1}{\kappa}\left(1-\lambda(1-e^{-1/\lambda})\right)+o(\kappa^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">1.2 ITP.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The weight is <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\textsf{ITP}}(\hat{r})=1+\hat{r}/\lambda=1+(1-U)/\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ITP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\textsf{ITP}}(\hat{r})=1+\hat{r}/\lambda=1+(1-U)/\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=1+1/\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=1+1/\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\textsf{i}}\propto C-U/\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">i</mtext></msub><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\textsf{i}}\propto C-U/\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Peak:</span>
The supremum is <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. The expectation is <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[w_{\textsf{i}}]=C-\mathbb{E}[U]/\lambda\approx C-\frac{1}{\lambda\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">i</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[w_{\textsf{i}}]=C-\mathbb{E}[U]/\lambda\approx C-\frac{1}{\lambda\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Peak}=\frac{C}{C-\frac{1}{\lambda\kappa}}=\frac{1}{1-\frac{1}{C\lambda\kappa}}\approx 1+\frac{1}{C\lambda\kappa}=1+\frac{1}{(\lambda+1)\kappa}+o(\kappa^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Peak</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Peak}=\frac{C}{C-\frac{1}{\lambda\kappa}}=\frac{1}{1-\frac{1}{C\lambda\kappa}}\approx 1+\frac{1}{C\lambda\kappa}=1+\frac{1}{(\lambda+1)\kappa}+o(\kappa^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dist and Gain:</span>
Using standard variance approximations for linear weights:</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Dist}\approx 1+\frac{1}{4(\lambda+1)^{2}\kappa}+o(\kappa^{-1}),\quad\Delta\approx\frac{1}{2\kappa(\lambda+1)}+o(\kappa^{-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Dist</mtext><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Dist}\approx 1+\frac{1}{4(\lambda+1)^{2}\kappa}+o(\kappa^{-1}),\quad\Delta\approx\frac{1}{2\kappa(\lambda+1)}+o(\kappa^{-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Part 2: Light-tail regime (small <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math> concentrates near 0.
Both soft-BoN (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>) and ITP (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\hat{r}/\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\hat{r}/\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) behave as <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\hat{r}/\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\hat{r}/\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> to the first order, and therefore they have similar terms of Peak and Dist.
The difference of the bound lies in the Gain.</p>
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Peak:</span> For <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\hat{r})=1+\hat{r}/\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\hat{r})=1+\hat{r}/\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup w=1+1/\lambda=\frac{\lambda+1}{\lambda},\quad\mathbb{E}[w]=1+\frac{\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}]}{\lambda}\approx 1+\frac{\kappa}{\lambda}=\frac{\lambda+\kappa}{\lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup w=1+1/\lambda=\frac{\lambda+1}{\lambda},\quad\mathbb{E}[w]=1+\frac{\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}]}{\lambda}\approx 1+\frac{\kappa}{\lambda}=\frac{\lambda+\kappa}{\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The Peak is:</p>
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Peak}=\frac{(\lambda+1)/\lambda}{(\lambda+\kappa)/\lambda}=\frac{\lambda+1}{\lambda+\kappa}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Peak</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Peak}=\frac{(\lambda+1)/\lambda}{(\lambda+\kappa)/\lambda}=\frac{\lambda+1}{\lambda+\kappa}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting into the bound exponent:</p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(-\frac{N}{\text{Peak}}\right)=\exp\left(-\frac{N(\lambda+\kappa)}{\lambda+1}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mtext>Peak</mtext></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(-\frac{N}{\text{Peak}}\right)=\exp\left(-\frac{N(\lambda+\kappa)}{\lambda+1}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dist.:</span> Using <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Var}(w)\approx\text{Var}(\hat{r})/\lambda^{2}\approx\kappa^{2}/\lambda^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Var}(w)\approx\text{Var}(\hat{r})/\lambda^{2}\approx\kappa^{2}/\lambda^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[w]\approx 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[w]\approx 1</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Dist}\approx 1+\frac{\text{Var}(w)}{2\mathbb{E}[w]^{2}}\approx 1+\frac{\kappa^{2}}{2\lambda^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Dist</mtext><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Dist}\approx 1+\frac{\text{Var}(w)}{2\mathbb{E}[w]^{2}}\approx 1+\frac{\kappa^{2}}{2\lambda^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">2.1 Soft-BoN.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gain</span> is given by <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{w}}[\hat{r}]=\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]/\mathbb{E}[e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{w}}[\hat{r}]=\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]/\mathbb{E}[e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Expanding the numerator <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}(1+\hat{r}/\lambda+\frac{1}{2\lambda^{2}}\hat{r}^{2}+O(\hat{r}^{3}))]=\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}]+\frac{1}{\lambda}\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}^{2}]+\frac{1}{2\lambda^{2}}\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}^{3}]+O(\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}^{4}])." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}(1+\hat{r}/\lambda+\frac{1}{2\lambda^{2}}\hat{r}^{2}+O(\hat{r}^{3}))]=\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}]+\frac{1}{\lambda}\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}^{2}]+\frac{1}{2\lambda^{2}}\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}^{3}]+O(\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}^{4}]).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By the moments of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math> with small <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]=\kappa+\frac{2\kappa^{2}}{\lambda}+\frac{3\kappa^{3}}{\lambda^{2}}+O(\kappa^{4})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]=\kappa+\frac{2\kappa^{2}}{\lambda}+\frac{3\kappa^{3}}{\lambda^{2}}+O(\kappa^{4}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">while the denominator expands as <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]=1+\frac{\kappa}{\lambda}+\frac{\kappa^{2}}{\lambda^{2}}+O(\kappa^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]=1+\frac{\kappa}{\lambda}+\frac{\kappa^{2}}{\lambda^{2}}+O(\kappa^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. Performing a ratio expansion then yields <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{w}}[\hat{r}]=\kappa+\frac{\kappa^{2}}{\lambda}+\frac{\kappa^{3}}{\lambda^{2}}+O(\kappa^{4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{w}}[\hat{r}]=\kappa+\frac{\kappa^{2}}{\lambda}+\frac{\kappa^{3}}{\lambda^{2}}+O(\kappa^{4})</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, subtracting the reference mean <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}]=\kappa+O(\kappa^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}]=\kappa+O(\kappa^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> gives the proxy gain</p>
<table id="A1.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\frac{\kappa^{2}}{\lambda}+\frac{\kappa^{3}}{\lambda^{2}}+O(\kappa^{4})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\frac{\kappa^{2}}{\lambda}+\frac{\kappa^{3}}{\lambda^{2}}+O(\kappa^{4}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">2.2 ITP.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gain</span> is dominated by the covariance term:</p>
<table id="A1.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\frac{\text{Cov}(w,\hat{r})}{\mathbb{E}[w]}\approx\frac{\text{Var}(\hat{r})/\lambda}{1}\approx\frac{\kappa^{2}}{\lambda}+O(\kappa^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\frac{\text{Cov}(w,\hat{r})}{\mathbb{E}[w]}\approx\frac{\text{Var}(\hat{r})/\lambda}{1}\approx\frac{\kappa^{2}}{\lambda}+O(\kappa^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Part 3: BoN limit (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Best-of-<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> (BoN) arises as the limit of Soft-BoN as the inverse temperature <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\lambda\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\lambda\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the supremum of the weights is <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{y}w_{\mathrm{soft}}(\hat{r}(x,y))=e^{1/\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>soft</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{y}w_{\mathrm{soft}}(\hat{r}(x,y))=e^{1/\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> and the normalizing constant <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]</annotation></semantics></math> remains finite for any fixed <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, the peak ratio diverges as <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Peak}(w_{\mathrm{soft}};x)=e^{1/\lambda}/\mathbb{E}[e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Peak</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>soft</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Peak}(w_{\mathrm{soft}};x)=e^{1/\lambda}/\mathbb{E}[e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, the distortion diverges as <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Dist}(w_{\mathrm{soft}};x)=\sqrt{\mathbb{E}[e^{2\hat{r}/\lambda}]}/\mathbb{E}[e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>soft</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Dist}(w_{\mathrm{soft}};x)=\sqrt{\mathbb{E}[e^{2\hat{r}/\lambda}]}/\mathbb{E}[e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. In the light-tail regime, the expansion <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]=1+\kappa/\lambda+\kappa^{2}/\lambda^{2}+O(\kappa^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[e^{\hat{r}/\lambda}]=1+\kappa/\lambda+\kappa^{2}/\lambda^{2}+O(\kappa^{3})</annotation></semantics></math> implies that the peak scales as <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Peak}(w_{\mathrm{soft}};x)\asymp e^{1/\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Peak</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>soft</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≍</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Peak}(w_{\mathrm{soft}};x)\asymp e^{1/\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, minimizing the finite-<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> proxy term <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\exp(-N/\mathrm{Peak})\approx 2\exp(-N/e^{1/\lambda})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>Peak</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\exp(-N/\mathrm{Peak})\approx 2\exp(-N/e^{1/\lambda})</annotation></semantics></math> requires the sample size <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> to scale on the order of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{1/\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{1/\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, confirming the qualitative behavior of BoN.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Combining Parts 1-3 completes the proof.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmprop3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Consider the generator function <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\alpha}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\alpha}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> of the <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-Tsallis divergence</p>
<table id="A1.E32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E32X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phi_{\alpha}(t)=\frac{t^{\alpha}-\alpha t+(\alpha-1)}{\alpha(\alpha-1)},\;t&gt;0,\alpha&gt;1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phi_{\alpha}(t)=\frac{t^{\alpha}-\alpha t+(\alpha-1)}{\alpha(\alpha-1)},\;t&gt;0,\alpha&gt;1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then, the <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-Tsallis divergence between two distributions <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> can be alternatively expressed as <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\alpha}(P\|Q)=\sum\limits_{x\in{\mathcal{X}}}Q(x)\phi_{\alpha}\left(\frac{P(x)}{Q(x)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\alpha}(P\|Q)=\sum\limits_{x\in{\mathcal{X}}}Q(x)\phi_{\alpha}\left(\frac{P(x)}{Q(x)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\alpha}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\alpha}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is convex with <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\alpha}(1)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\alpha}(1)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is also convex in <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now, let the tilting function be <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(y|x)=\pi(y|x)/\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(y|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(y|x)=\pi(y|x)/\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(y|x)</annotation></semantics></math>, the objective in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) becomes</p>
<table id="A1.E33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E33X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{\alpha}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{L}}_{\alpha}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}(x,y)\right]-\lambda D_{\alpha}\left(\pi(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(\cdot|x)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}\left[\hat{r}(x,y)\right]-\lambda D_{\alpha}\left(\pi(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(\cdot|x)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.33)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E33Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\pi(y|x)\hat{r}(x,y)-\lambda\sum\limits_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(y|x)\phi_{\alpha}\left(\frac{\pi(y|x)}{\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(y|x)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\pi(y|x)\hat{r}(x,y)-\lambda\sum\limits_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(y|x)\phi_{\alpha}\left(\frac{\pi(y|x)}{\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(y|x)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E33Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(y|x)\left(t(y|x)\hat{r}(x,y)-\lambda\phi_{\alpha}(t(y|x))\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum\limits_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(y|x)\left(t(y|x)\hat{r}(x,y)-\lambda\phi_{\alpha}(t(y|x))\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The simplex constraint <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\pi(y|x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\pi(y|x)=1</annotation></semantics></math> becomes <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(y|x)t(y|x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(y|x)t(y|x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
The transformation in Eq. (<a href="#A1.E33" title="Equation A.33 ‣ A.3 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Omitted Proofs and Theoretical Results ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.33</span></a>) actually forms the convex conjugate (Fenchel–Legendre transform) of the generator function, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A1.E34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E34X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi_{\alpha}(z)=\sup\limits_{t&gt;0}\left\{zt-\lambda\phi_{\alpha}(t)\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi_{\alpha}(z)=\sup\limits_{t&gt;0}\left\{zt-\lambda\phi_{\alpha}(t)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">The optimizer <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}(z)=\argmax\limits_{t&gt;0}zt-\lambda\phi_{\alpha}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mi>zt</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}(z)=\argmax\limits_{t&gt;0}zt-\lambda\phi_{\alpha}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> can then be derived directly from the first-order condition</p>
<table id="A1.E35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E35X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}(zt-\phi_{\alpha}(t)\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}(zt-\phi_{\alpha}(t)\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=z-\lambda\phi_{\alpha}^{\prime}(t)=z-\lambda\frac{1}{\alpha(\alpha-1)}(\alpha t^{\alpha-1}-\alpha)=z-\lambda\frac{t^{\alpha-1}-1}{\alpha-1}=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=z-\lambda\phi_{\alpha}^{\prime}(t)=z-\lambda\frac{1}{\alpha(\alpha-1)}(\alpha t^{\alpha-1}-\alpha)=z-\lambda\frac{t^{\alpha-1}-1}{\alpha-1}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">By re-arranging and plugging <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\hat{r}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\hat{r}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\alpha-1}=1+\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda}\hat{r}(x,y)\Rightarrow t^{*}(\hat{r}(x,y))=\left[1+(\alpha-1)\frac{\hat{r}(x,y)}{\lambda}\right]_{+}^{\frac{1}{\alpha-1}}=\exp_{\alpha}\left(\frac{\hat{r}(x,y)}{\lambda}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>exp</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\alpha-1}=1+\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda}\hat{r}(x,y)\Rightarrow t^{*}(\hat{r}(x,y))=\left[1+(\alpha-1)\frac{\hat{r}(x,y)}{\lambda}\right]_{+}^{\frac{1}{\alpha-1}}=\exp_{\alpha}\left(\frac{\hat{r}(x,y)}{\lambda}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">and therefore</p>
<table id="A1.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\alpha}(\cdot|x)\propto\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(\cdot|x)\exp_{\alpha}\left(\frac{\hat{r}(x,y)}{\lambda}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>exp</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\alpha}(\cdot|x)\propto\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(\cdot|x)\exp_{\alpha}\left(\frac{\hat{r}(x,y)}{\lambda}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.8" class="ltx_p">The simplex condition <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\pi_{\alpha}(y|x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\pi_{\alpha}(y|x)=1</annotation></semantics></math> can be satisfied by finding a <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\limits_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(y|x)t^{*}(\hat{r}(x,y)+\nu)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\limits_{y\in{\mathcal{Y}}}\pi_{\textsf{ref}}(y|x)t^{*}(\hat{r}(x,y)+\nu)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmprop4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ 4.1 Deciding the Prompt-Dependent 𝛼(𝑥) ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We proceed in three parts.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Part 1: Algebraic reductions.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U:=1-\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U:=1-\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and note <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}=1-U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}=1-U</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the parameters from the proposition statement: <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(1,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(1,2]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. The weight function is:</p>
<table id="A1.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\alpha}(\hat{r})=\left[1+(\alpha-1)\frac{\hat{r}}{\lambda}\right]_{+}^{\frac{1}{\alpha-1}}=\left(1+\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda}(1-U)\right)^{\frac{1}{\alpha-1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\alpha}(\hat{r})=\left[1+(\alpha-1)\frac{\hat{r}}{\lambda}\right]_{+}^{\frac{1}{\alpha-1}}=\left(1+\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda}(1-U)\right)^{\frac{1}{\alpha-1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We factor out the endpoint value at <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}=1</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=0</annotation></semantics></math>).
Define the constants:</p>
<table id="A1.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=1+\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda},\;\rho:=\frac{(\alpha-1)/\lambda}{1+(\alpha-1)/\lambda}=\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda A},\;\gamma:=\frac{1}{\alpha-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=1+\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda},\;\rho:=\frac{(\alpha-1)/\lambda}{1+(\alpha-1)/\lambda}=\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda A},\;\gamma:=\frac{1}{\alpha-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then we can rewrite the inner term as:</p>
<table id="A1.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda}(1-U)=1+\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda}-\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda}U=A-A\rho U=A(1-\rho U)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda}(1-U)=1+\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda}-\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda}U=A-A\rho U=A(1-\rho U).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the weight becomes:</p>
<table id="A1.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\alpha}(1-U)=\left(A(1-\rho U)\right)^{\gamma}=A^{\gamma}(1-\rho U)^{\gamma}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\alpha}(1-U)=\left(A(1-\rho U)\right)^{\gamma}=A^{\gamma}(1-\rho U)^{\gamma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The moments of the weights under the reference distribution (parameterized by <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>) are:</p>
<table id="A1.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[w_{\alpha}(\hat{r})]=A^{\gamma}\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[(1-\rho U)^{\gamma}]=A^{\gamma}m_{0},\;\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[w_{\alpha}(\hat{r})^{2}]=A^{2\gamma}\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[(1-\rho U)^{2\gamma}]=A^{2\gamma}m_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[w_{\alpha}(\hat{r})]=A^{\gamma}\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[(1-\rho U)^{\gamma}]=A^{\gamma}m_{0},\;\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[w_{\alpha}(\hat{r})^{2}]=A^{2\gamma}\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[(1-\rho U)^{2\gamma}]=A^{2\gamma}m_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where we define <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}(\alpha;\kappa,\lambda):=\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[(1-\rho U)^{\gamma}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}(\alpha;\kappa,\lambda):=\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[(1-\rho U)^{\gamma}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{2}(\alpha;\kappa,\lambda):=\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[(1-\rho U)^{2\gamma}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{2}(\alpha;\kappa,\lambda):=\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[(1-\rho U)^{2\gamma}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, the distortion ratio simplifies to:</p>
<table id="A1.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{|w_{\alpha}|{L^{2}}}{|w_{\alpha}|{L^{1}}}=\frac{\sqrt{\mathbb{E}\kappa[w_{\alpha}(\hat{r})^{2}]}}{\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[w_{\alpha}(\hat{r})]}=\frac{\sqrt{A^{2\gamma}m_{2}}}{A^{\gamma}m_{0}}=\frac{\sqrt{m_{2}}}{m_{0}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{|w_{\alpha}|{L^{2}}}{|w_{\alpha}|{L^{1}}}=\frac{\sqrt{\mathbb{E}\kappa[w_{\alpha}(\hat{r})^{2}]}}{\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[w_{\alpha}(\hat{r})]}=\frac{\sqrt{A^{2\gamma}m_{2}}}{A^{\gamma}m_{0}}=\frac{\sqrt{m_{2}}}{m_{0}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\alpha}(\hat{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\alpha}(\hat{r})</annotation></semantics></math> is increasing in <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, its supremum is at <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup w_{\alpha}=A^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup w_{\alpha}=A^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The envelope constant for the exponential mechanism is:</p>
<table id="A1.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\alpha)=\frac{\sup w_{\alpha}}{\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[w_{\alpha}]}=\frac{A^{\gamma}}{A^{\gamma}m_{0}}=\frac{1}{m_{0}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\alpha)=\frac{\sup w_{\alpha}}{\mathbb{E}_{\kappa}[w_{\alpha}]}=\frac{A^{\gamma}}{A^{\gamma}m_{0}}=\frac{1}{m_{0}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The probability of selecting the reference policy is <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-NM(\alpha)^{-1}}=e^{-Nm_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-NM(\alpha)^{-1}}=e^{-Nm_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This yields the first term in (<a href="#S4.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Proposition 4. ‣ 4.1 Deciding the Prompt-Dependent 𝛼(𝑥) ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>).
The proxy gain is:</p>
<table id="A1.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\pi_{\textsf{BoT}})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\alpha}}[\hat{r}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textsf{ref}}}[\hat{r}]=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textsf{ref}}}[U]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\alpha}}[U]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">BoT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\pi_{\textsf{BoT}})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\alpha}}[\hat{r}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textsf{ref}}}[\hat{r}]=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textsf{ref}}}[U]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\alpha}}[U],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where we used <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}=1-U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}=1-U</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Part 2: Heavy-tailed regime (large <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the heavy-tailed regime (<math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> concentrates near <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\sim\text{Beta}(1/\kappa,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Beta</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\sim\text{Beta}(1/\kappa,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the moments <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[U]=\frac{1}{\kappa+1}=\frac{1}{\kappa}-\frac{1}{\kappa^{2}}+O(\kappa^{-3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[U]=\frac{1}{\kappa+1}=\frac{1}{\kappa}-\frac{1}{\kappa^{2}}+O(\kappa^{-3})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]=\frac{1}{2\kappa+1}=\frac{1}{2\kappa}+O(\kappa^{-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]=\frac{1}{2\kappa+1}=\frac{1}{2\kappa}+O(\kappa^{-2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We expand <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\rho U)^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\rho U)^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> around <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\rho U)^{\gamma}=1-\gamma\rho U+\frac{\gamma(\gamma-1)}{2}\rho^{2}U^{2}+O(U^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\rho U)^{\gamma}=1-\gamma\rho U+\frac{\gamma(\gamma-1)}{2}\rho^{2}U^{2}+O(U^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Taking expectations:</p>
<table id="A1.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}=1-\gamma\rho\mathbb{E}[U]+\frac{\gamma(\gamma-1)}{2}\rho^{2}\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]+O(\kappa^{-2})=1+\frac{1}{\kappa}\left(-\gamma\rho+\frac{\gamma(\gamma-1)}{4}\rho^{2}\right)+O(\kappa^{-2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}=1-\gamma\rho\mathbb{E}[U]+\frac{\gamma(\gamma-1)}{2}\rho^{2}\mathbb{E}[U^{2}]+O(\kappa^{-2})=1+\frac{1}{\kappa}\left(-\gamma\rho+\frac{\gamma(\gamma-1)}{4}\rho^{2}\right)+O(\kappa^{-2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{1}{\alpha-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{1}{\alpha-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\frac{(\alpha-1)/\lambda}{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\frac{(\alpha-1)/\lambda}{A}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\rho=\frac{1}{\alpha-1}\cdot\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda A}=\frac{1}{\lambda A}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\rho=\frac{1}{\alpha-1}\cdot\frac{\alpha-1}{\lambda A}=\frac{1}{\lambda A}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The quadratic coefficient involves <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(\gamma-1)=\frac{1}{\alpha-1}(\frac{1}{\alpha-1}-1)=\frac{2-\alpha}{(\alpha-1)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(\gamma-1)=\frac{1}{\alpha-1}(\frac{1}{\alpha-1}-1)=\frac{2-\alpha}{(\alpha-1)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus:</p>
<table id="A1.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\gamma(\gamma-1)}{4}\rho^{2}=\frac{2-\alpha}{4(\alpha-1)^{2}}\frac{(\alpha-1)^{2}}{\lambda^{2}A^{2}}=\frac{2-\alpha}{4\lambda^{2}A^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\gamma(\gamma-1)}{4}\rho^{2}=\frac{2-\alpha}{4(\alpha-1)^{2}}\frac{(\alpha-1)^{2}}{\lambda^{2}A^{2}}=\frac{2-\alpha}{4\lambda^{2}A^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Combining these over a common denominator <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\lambda^{2}A^{2}=4(\lambda+\alpha-1)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\lambda^{2}A^{2}=4(\lambda+\alpha-1)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}=1+\frac{1}{\kappa}\frac{-4\lambda A+2-\alpha}{4\lambda^{2}A^{2}}+O(\kappa^{-2})=1+\frac{1}{\kappa}\frac{-4\lambda-5(\alpha-1)+1}{4(\lambda+\alpha-1)^{2}}+O(\kappa^{-2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}=1+\frac{1}{\kappa}\frac{-4\lambda A+2-\alpha}{4\lambda^{2}A^{2}}+O(\kappa^{-2})=1+\frac{1}{\kappa}\frac{-4\lambda-5(\alpha-1)+1}{4(\lambda+\alpha-1)^{2}}+O(\kappa^{-2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">The finite-<math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> term expands as <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-Nm_{0}}\approx e^{-N}(1-N(m_{0}-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-Nm_{0}}\approx e^{-N}(1-N(m_{0}-1))</annotation></semantics></math>, contributing the term matching (<a href="#S4.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ 1st item ‣ Proposition 4. ‣ 4.1 Deciding the Prompt-Dependent 𝛼(𝑥) ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Expanding <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{2}=\mathbb{E}[(1-\rho U)^{2\gamma}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{2}=\mathbb{E}[(1-\rho U)^{2\gamma}]</annotation></semantics></math> similarly leads to <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{2}=1+\frac{1}{\kappa}(-2\gamma\rho+\frac{2\gamma(2\gamma-1)}{4}\rho^{2})+O(\kappa^{-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{2}=1+\frac{1}{\kappa}(-2\gamma\rho+\frac{2\gamma(2\gamma-1)}{4}\rho^{2})+O(\kappa^{-2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The ratio <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{m_{2}}/m_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{m_{2}}/m_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> expands as:</p>
<table id="A1.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sqrt{m_{2}}}{m_{0}}\approx 1+\frac{1}{\kappa}\left(\frac{1}{2}\text{coeff}(m_{2})-\text{coeff}(m_{0})\right)=1+\frac{1}{\kappa}\frac{\gamma^{2}\rho^{2}}{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>coeff</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>coeff</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sqrt{m_{2}}}{m_{0}}\approx 1+\frac{1}{\kappa}\left(\frac{1}{2}\text{coeff}(m_{2})-\text{coeff}(m_{0})\right)=1+\frac{1}{\kappa}\frac{\gamma^{2}\rho^{2}}{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\rho=\frac{1}{\lambda+\alpha-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\rho=\frac{1}{\lambda+\alpha-1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sqrt{m_{2}}}{m_{0}}=1+\frac{1}{4\kappa(\lambda+\alpha-1)^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sqrt{m_{2}}}{m_{0}}=1+\frac{1}{4\kappa(\lambda+\alpha-1)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">This yields the first term in (<a href="#S4.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ 1st item ‣ Proposition 4. ‣ 4.1 Deciding the Prompt-Dependent 𝛼(𝑥) ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We compute <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\pi_{\textsf{BoT}})=\mathbb{E}[U]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\alpha}}[U]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">BoT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\pi_{\textsf{BoT}})=\mathbb{E}[U]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\alpha}}[U]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using the integral approximation for large <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\alpha}}[U]=\frac{1}{\kappa}\int_{0}^{1}(1-\rho u)^{\gamma}du+O(\kappa^{-2})=\frac{1}{\kappa}\frac{1-(1-\rho)^{\gamma+1}}{\rho(\gamma+1)}+O(\kappa^{-2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\alpha}}[U]=\frac{1}{\kappa}\int_{0}^{1}(1-\rho u)^{\gamma}du+O(\kappa^{-2})=\frac{1}{\kappa}\frac{1-(1-\rho)^{\gamma+1}}{\rho(\gamma+1)}+O(\kappa^{-2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Linearizing near <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=2</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1</annotation></semantics></math>), the integral is <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\rho/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\rho/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus:</p>
<table id="A1.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\pi_{\textsf{BoT}})\approx\frac{1}{\kappa}-\frac{1}{\kappa}(1-\rho/2)=\frac{\rho}{2\kappa}=\frac{1}{\kappa}\frac{\alpha-1}{2(\lambda+\alpha-1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">BoT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\pi_{\textsf{BoT}})\approx\frac{1}{\kappa}-\frac{1}{\kappa}(1-\rho/2)=\frac{\rho}{2\kappa}=\frac{1}{\kappa}\frac{\alpha-1}{2(\lambda+\alpha-1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">This matches the final term in (<a href="#S4.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ 1st item ‣ Proposition 4. ‣ 4.1 Deciding the Prompt-Dependent 𝛼(𝑥) ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Part 3: Light-tailed regime (small <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this regime (<math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math> concentrates near <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.
From <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\sim\text{Beta}(1/\kappa,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Beta</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\sim\text{Beta}(1/\kappa,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}=1-U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}=1-U</annotation></semantics></math> has moments:</p>
<table id="A1.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}]\approx\kappa-\kappa^{2}+\kappa^{3},\quad\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}^{2}]\approx 2\kappa^{2}-6\kappa^{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}]\approx\kappa-\kappa^{2}+\kappa^{3},\quad\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}^{2}]\approx 2\kappa^{2}-6\kappa^{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using the expansion <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\alpha}(\hat{r})\approx 1+\frac{\hat{r}}{\lambda}+\frac{2-\alpha}{2\lambda^{2}}\hat{r}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\alpha}(\hat{r})\approx 1+\frac{\hat{r}}{\lambda}+\frac{2-\alpha}{2\lambda^{2}}\hat{r}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[w_{\alpha}]\approx 1+\frac{\kappa}{\lambda}+\kappa^{2}\left(\frac{2-\alpha}{\lambda^{2}}-\frac{1}{\lambda}\right),\;\mathbb{E}[w_{\alpha}^{2}]\approx 1+\frac{2\kappa}{\lambda}+\kappa^{2}\left(\frac{2(3-\alpha)}{\lambda^{2}}-\frac{2}{\lambda}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[w_{\alpha}]\approx 1+\frac{\kappa}{\lambda}+\kappa^{2}\left(\frac{2-\alpha}{\lambda^{2}}-\frac{1}{\lambda}\right),\;\mathbb{E}[w_{\alpha}^{2}]\approx 1+\frac{2\kappa}{\lambda}+\kappa^{2}\left(\frac{2(3-\alpha)}{\lambda^{2}}-\frac{2}{\lambda}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The gain <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\alpha}}[\hat{r}]-\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\alpha}}[\hat{r}]-\mathbb{E}[\hat{r}]</annotation></semantics></math> is dominated by the covariance term <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Cov}(w_{\alpha},\hat{r})/\mathbb{E}[w_{\alpha}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Cov}(w_{\alpha},\hat{r})/\mathbb{E}[w_{\alpha}]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\alpha}}[\hat{r}]\approx\kappa+\frac{\kappa^{2}}{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\alpha}}[\hat{r}]\approx\kappa+\frac{\kappa^{2}}{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\approx\frac{\kappa^{2}}{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\approx\frac{\kappa^{2}}{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Including higher order terms leads to the expansion in (<a href="#S4.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ 2nd item ‣ Proposition 4. ‣ 4.1 Deciding the Prompt-Dependent 𝛼(𝑥) ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>).
The squared distortion is:</p>
<table id="A1.E57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Dist}^{2}=\frac{\mathbb{E}[w_{\alpha}^{2}]}{\mathbb{E}[w_{\alpha}]^{2}}\approx 1+\frac{\kappa^{2}}{\lambda^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext>Dist</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Dist}^{2}=\frac{\mathbb{E}[w_{\alpha}^{2}]}{\mathbb{E}[w_{\alpha}]^{2}}\approx 1+\frac{\kappa^{2}}{\lambda^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Taking the square root yields <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Dist}\approx 1+\frac{\kappa^{2}}{2\lambda^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Dist</mtext><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Dist}\approx 1+\frac{\kappa^{2}}{2\lambda^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Combining these expansions yields the asymptotic results stated in the proposition.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Discussion and Experimental Setup</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We detail the Hill estimator in § <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Practical Implementation ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, elucidating its sample complexity advantages over estimating the entire reward distribution and outlining our experimental implementation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Tail Estimation via the Hill Estimator</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To implement the prompt-adaptive strategy, we require a robust estimate of the tail index <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(x)</annotation></semantics></math> from a finite set of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> candidate responses.
We adopt the Hill estimator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hill, 1975</a>)</cite>, the standard semi-parametric estimator for heavy-tailed distributions.
Standard extreme value theory typically deals with unbounded random variables; however, our proxy rewards are bounded, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}(x,y)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}(x,y)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
To bridge this, we analyze the reward gaps (or regrets):</p>
<table id="A2.E58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(x,y)=1-\hat{r}(x,y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(x,y)=1-\hat{r}(x,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The “tail” of the reward distribution (where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}\approx 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}\approx 1</annotation></semantics></math>) corresponds to the limit <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
As established in our modeling assumption (Prop. <a href="#Thmprop2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ 3.2 Light vs. Heavy Tails: When to be Optimistic? ‣ 3 Reward Tails and Alignment Regret ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), the tail behavior is characterized by <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(U\leq u)\approx u^{1/\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(U\leq u)\approx u^{1/\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By applying the transformation <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=1/U=(1-\hat{r})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=1/U=(1-\hat{r})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we map the problem to a standard Pareto tail estimation where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr(Z&gt;z)=\Pr(U&lt;1/z)\approx z^{-1/\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(Z&gt;z)=\Pr(U&lt;1/z)\approx z^{-1/\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> appears precisely as the shape parameter (tail index) of the resulting Pareto distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> sampled responses, let <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{(1)}\geq r_{(2)}\geq\dots\geq r_{(N)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{(1)}\geq r_{(2)}\geq\dots\geq r_{(N)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the order statistics of the rewards.
These correspond to the ordered transformed variables <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{(1)}\geq Z_{(2)}\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{(1)}\geq Z_{(2)}\dots</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{(i)}=(1-r_{(i)})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{(i)}=(1-r_{(i)})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The Hill estimator uses the top <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> order statistics to estimate <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E59X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E59X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E59X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\log\left(\frac{Z_{(i)}}{Z_{(K+1)}}\right)=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\log\left(\frac{(1-r_{(i)})^{-1}}{(1-r_{(K+1)})^{-1}}\right)=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\log\left(\frac{1-r_{(K+1)}}{1-r_{(i)}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\log\left(\frac{Z_{(i)}}{Z_{(K+1)}}\right)=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\log\left(\frac{(1-r_{(i)})^{-1}}{(1-r_{(K+1)})^{-1}}\right)=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\log\left(\frac{1-r_{(K+1)}}{1-r_{(i)}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(A.59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The hyperparameter <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> determines the “tail cut-off”—the boundary between the distribution’s tail and its body.</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Small <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>: Uses only the most extreme data points. This minimizes bias (as the asymptotic tail approximation is most accurate here) but increases variance due to the small sample size.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Large <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>: Incorporates more samples, reducing variance. However, if <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is too large, it includes samples from the central body of the distribution where the power-law assumption fails, introducing significant bias.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">In <span id="A2.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BoT</span>, we fix <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> to a small fraction of <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\approx\sqrt{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≈</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\approx\sqrt{N}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\%-10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\%-10\%</annotation></semantics></math>) to prioritize low bias, ensuring <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(x)</annotation></semantics></math> reacts only to the true extremal behavior of the prompt.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Sample Complexity: Tail Index vs. Full Distribution</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A fundamental advantage of the <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BoT</span> framework is that it adapts to the reward landscape without requiring a full estimate of the reward distribution.
Estimating the complete probability density function <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(r)</annotation></semantics></math> is a non-parametric problem subject to the curse of dimensionality and slow convergence rates.
In contrast, estimating the tail index <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> is a semi-parametric problem that enjoys faster statistical convergence.
We formalize this distinction below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the task of estimating the underlying reward density <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(r)</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> samples to within an error <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> in total variation distance or <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm.
The minimax convergence rate for estimating a generic smooth density (Hölder class <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma(\beta,L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma(\beta,L)</annotation></semantics></math>) in <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math> dimension is</p>
<table id="A2.E60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{\hat{p}}\sup_{p\in\Sigma}\mathbb{E}\left[|\hat{p}-p|\right]\asymp N^{-\frac{\beta}{2\beta+1}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≍</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{\hat{p}}\sup_{p\in\Sigma}\mathbb{E}\left[|\hat{p}-p|\right]\asymp N^{-\frac{\beta}{2\beta+1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is the smoothness parameter.
For typical values (e.g., <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=2</annotation></semantics></math>), this yields a rate of <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N^{-2/5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{-2/5}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is significantly slower than the parametric rate <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This implies that accurately characterizing the entire reward landscape to optimize a policy would require a prohibitively large number of samples <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Conversely, <span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BoT</span> relies only on the tail index <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, a single scalar summary of the extreme value behavior.
Under standard Second-Order Regular Variation conditions, the Hill estimator <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> (using the top <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> statistics) is asymptotically normal <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">De Haan and Resnick, 1998</a>)</cite>:</p>
<table id="A2.E61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{K}\left(\hat{\kappa}_{K}-\kappa\right)\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}(0,\kappa^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{K}\left(\hat{\kappa}_{K}-\kappa\right)\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}(0,\kappa^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This indicates that the estimation error decays at the parametric rate <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/\sqrt{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/\sqrt{K})</annotation></semantics></math>. Crucially, the sample complexity to estimate <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> to a fixed precision <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the number of <em id="A2.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">tail samples</em> <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, not the complexity of the full distribution’s support.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In our design, <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(x)</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ 4.2 Practical Implementation ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>)) is a smooth, bounded monotonic function of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, we do not need infinite precision in <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We essentially perform a “soft classification” of the tail regime (heavy vs. light).
The sample complexity to distinguish these regimes is low; even with moderate sample sizes (e.g., <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\approx 50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\approx 50</annotation></semantics></math>), the variance of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently small to steer <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(x)</annotation></semantics></math> towards the correct end of the interval <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,2]</annotation></semantics></math>.
This makes <span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BoT</span> highly sample-efficient compared to methods that might attempt to model the full reward surface.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct a comprehensive empirical analysis across a diverse suite of reasoning and instruction-following tasks. Our evaluation protocol encompasses four standard benchmarks, three instruction-tuned reference policies, and four diverse reward models.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate performance on the following four benchmarks:</p>
<ol id="A2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GSM8K (Grade School Math) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>)</cite>: A standard benchmark for multi-step mathematical reasoning. We utilize the test split, comprising 1,319 high-quality grade-school math problems with integer answers. We define the oracle reward <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\star}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\star}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> as a binary metric: <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\star}(x,y)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\star}(x,y)=1</annotation></semantics></math> if the final numerical answer is correct, and 0 otherwise.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">MMLU (Massive Multitask Language Understanding) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al., 2021a</a>)</cite>: To assess knowledge-intensive reasoning in specialized STEM domains, we utilize the <em id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">College Mathematics</em> and <em id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">College Chemistry</em> test splits (approx. 100 questions each). Unlike GSM8K, these tasks use a multiple-choice format. Correctness is determined by matching the model’s final selection to the ground truth key.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">MATH (Mathematics Aptitude Test of Heuristics) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al., 2021b</a>)</cite>: For competition-level mathematics requiring complex heuristics, we construct an evaluation set by randomly sampling 512 instances from the MATH test split. These problems are more challenging, and require complex heuristic application and advanced reasoning beyond standard grade-school arithmetic. Similar to GSM8K, the oracle reward is binary based on the exact match of the final calculated result.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">AlpacaFarm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dubois et al., 2023</a>)</cite>: Designed to simulate ”in-the-wild” interactions, this dataset covers diverse tasks from creative writing to open-ended QA. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Coste et al. (2024)</a></cite>, we use the standard test set of 805 prompts. Since open-ended tasks lack verifiable ground truth, we employ <span id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Alpaca-RM</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dubois et al., 2023</a>)</cite>—fine-tuned from LLaMA-7B on human preference data—as the oracle reward <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> for evaluation.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the reasoning tasks (GSM8K, MMLU, MATH) with verifiable ground truth, we consider three instruction-tuned reference policies (<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\textsf{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\textsf{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>): <span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Gemma-2-2B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gemma et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, <span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-3-3B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grattafiori et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and <span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Mistral-7B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.
For AlpacaFarm, we follow prior work and use the <span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Pythia-1.4B</span> model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Biderman et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We pair these policies with four diverse proxy reward models (<math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<ol id="A2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">OASST-RM</span> (1.4B): Based on Pythia-1.4B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Köpf et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Gemma-RM</span> (2B): Trained from <span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">google/gemma-2b-it</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dong et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-RM</span> (3B): A generalizable RM trained from <span id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">meta/llama-3.2-3B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ARMO-RM</span> (8B): A mixture-of-experts model trained from <span id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">meta/llama-3-8B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We prompt all reference policies using zero-shot Chain-of-Thought (CoT) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wei et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, i.e., without any in-context demonstrations, to elicit reasoning.
To maximize response diversity, we set the temperature to 1.0 and top-<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> to 1.0 (no nucleus sampling), limiting generation to 512 tokens.
For each unique combination of dataset, policy, and reward model, we pre-generate a large candidate pool of <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{12}=4,096" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>12</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4,096</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{12}=4,096</annotation></semantics></math> responses per prompt.
For AlpacaFarm, we generate 12,600 responses per prompt following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Coste et al., 2024</a></cite>.
We simulate experiments by bootstrapping subsets of varying size <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> from this pool, reporting results averaged over 10 independent trials to ensure statistical robustness.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For the Hill estimator (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ 4.2 Practical Implementation ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>)) in <span id="A2.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BoT</span>, we adaptively set the tail cutoff as <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\max(1,\sqrt{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\max(1,\sqrt{N})</annotation></semantics></math> to balance bias and variance as <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> scales.
To calibrate the mapping function <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we select the pivot <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> based on the reward model’s typical behavior; specifically, we set <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to the median of the estimated tail indices <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{\kappa}(x_{i})\}_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{\kappa}(x_{i})\}_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> over the set of <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> prompts. This centers the sigmoid mapping, preventing the policy from saturating into purely optimistic or pessimistic modes, and ensuring <span id="A2.SS3.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BoT</span> remains sensitive to relative tail risk variations across prompts.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Experiments and Ablation Studies</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We include additional experimental results and comparisons, including: (i) comprehensive results of all configurations of the reference policies and reward models for each datasets, similar to Figures <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4.1 Deciding the Prompt-Dependent 𝛼(𝑥) ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 5 Empirical Study ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> in the main text; (ii) additional results of selected configurations in Figures <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4.1 Deciding the Prompt-Dependent 𝛼(𝑥) ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, including true reward <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, proxy reward <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. and the proxy reward over distortions (i.e., the RLHF objective in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>)); (iii) ablation studies on the steering temperature <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and tail pivot <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.1 Deciding the Prompt-Dependent 𝛼(𝑥) ‣ 4 BoT: A Tail-Adaptive Alignment ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>The Complete Results over all Datasets, Reference Policies, and Reward Models</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show the trajectory of the true reward (<math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>) versus the proxy reward (<math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math>) as the sample size <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> scales exponentially from <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{10}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\{2^{0}.2^{1},\cdots,2^{9},2^{10}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>.2</mn><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>10</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\{2^{0}.2^{1},\cdots,2^{9},2^{10}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
These detailed results span all combinations of reference policies and reward models, i.e., { <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Gemma-2-2B</span>, <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-3-3B</span>, <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Mistral-7B</span> } <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> { <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">OASST-RM</span>, <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Gemma-RM</span>, <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-RM</span>, <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ARMO-RM</span> } for GSM8K (Figure <a href="#A3.F4" title="Figure A.4 ‣ C.1 The Complete Results over all Datasets, Reference Policies, and Reward Models ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiments and Ablation Studies ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>), MMLU (Figure <a href="#A3.F5" title="Figure A.5 ‣ C.1 The Complete Results over all Datasets, Reference Policies, and Reward Models ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiments and Ablation Studies ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>), MATH (Figure <a href="#A3.F6" title="Figure A.6 ‣ C.1 The Complete Results over all Datasets, Reference Policies, and Reward Models ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiments and Ablation Studies ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>), and { <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Pythia-1.4B</span>} <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> { <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">OASST-RM</span>, <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Gemma-RM</span>, <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-RM</span>, <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ARMO-RM</span> } for AlpacaFarm (Figure <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure A.7 ‣ C.1 The Complete Results over all Datasets, Reference Policies, and Reward Models ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiments and Ablation Studies ‣ Best-of-Tails: Bridging Optimism and Pessimismin Inference-Time Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Across these configurations, we observe distinct failure modes for the baselines: optimistic strategies, such as <span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BoN</span> and <span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sBoN</span>, consistently succumb to reward hacking at large <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, while <span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ITP</span> remains overly conservative, often failing to adequately explore high-reward regions—a finding consistent with <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al. (2025b)</a></cite>. In contrast, <span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BoT</span> demonstrates robust adaptivity. Depending on the reward landscape, it either outperforms all baselines in high-variance regimes (e.g., <span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Mistral-7B</span>/<span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Gemma-RM</span> on MATH), matches the efficiency of <span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BoN</span> in light-tailed regime (e.g., <span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-3-3B</span>/<span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-RM</span> on MMLU), or converges to the safety of <span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ITP</span> when heavy-tailed rewards are dominant (e.g., <span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Gemma-2-2B</span>/<span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Gemma-RM</span> on GSM8K).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="A3.F4.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center ltx_align_center"><span id="A3.F4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2603.06797v1/app-figures/gsm8k-all-acc-vs-reward.png" id="A3.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/232;" width="429" height="232" alt="Refer to caption"></span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.4: </span><span id="A3.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of optimistic (<span id="A3.F4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sBoN</span>/<span id="A3.F4.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BoN</span>), pessimistic (<span id="A3.F4.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ITP</span>), and adaptive (<span id="A3.F4.4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BoT</span>) strategies on GSM8K across different reference models and proxy rewards.
Each curve traces the trajectory of True Reward (<math id="A3.F4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>) vs. Proxy Reward (<math id="A3.F4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math>) as the sample size <math id="A3.F4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> increases from <math id="A3.F4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.F4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{10}</annotation></semantics></math>, with marker size proportional to <math id="A3.F4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. The smallest marker represents <math id="A3.F4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1</annotation></semantics></math> (standard sampling), while the largest represents <math id="A3.F4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1024</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<figure id="A3.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="A3.F5.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center ltx_align_center"><span id="A3.F5.2.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2603.06797v1/app-figures/mmlu-all-acc-vs-reward.png" id="A3.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/232;" width="429" height="232" alt="Refer to caption"></span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.5: </span><span id="A3.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of optimistic (<span id="A3.F5.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sBoN</span>/<span id="A3.F5.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BoN</span>), pessimistic (<span id="A3.F5.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ITP</span>), and adaptive (<span id="A3.F5.4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">BoT</span>) strategies on MMLU across different reference models and proxy rewards.
Each curve traces the trajectory of True Reward (<math id="A3.F5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>) vs. Proxy Reward (<math id="A3.F5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math>) as the sample size <math id="A3.F5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> increases from <math id="A3.F5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.F5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{10}</annotation></semantics></math>, with marker size proportional to <math id="A3.F5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. The smallest marker represents <math id="A3.F5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1</annotation></semantics></math> (standard sampling), while the largest represents <math id="A3.F5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1024</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="A3.F6.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center ltx_align_center"><span id="A3.F6.2.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2603.06797v1/app-figures/math-all-acc-vs-reward.png" id="A3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/232;" width="429" height="232" alt="Refer to caption"></span></p>
